  "slug": "quantum-rydberg-6779",
  "summary": "Lattice-surgery teleportation on 41 superconducting qubits appears alongside proposals for color-code T gates, transversal ion CZ gates and finite-blockade CCZ.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is implementing logical and multi-qubit entangling operations across hardware platforms. The one experimental demonstration teleports logical qubits by lattice surgery between distance-three surface-code patches on 41 superconducting qubits. The remaining gate work consists of proposals addressing other fault-tolerance bottlenecks. A persistent-mediator architecture reuses a 3D color-code block to apply repeated logical T gates to a 2D register, supported by simulations. In a double-well trapped-ion architecture, parallel transversal CZ gates act across neighboring wells, combined with dynamical decoupling and crosstalk mitigation. A reset-assisted scheme uses noisy mediator qubits to drive high-fidelity gates on long-lived data qubits, analyzed with quantum trajectories. For neutral atoms, an analytically specified CCZ gate under finite Rydberg interactions is compared with a fast antiblockade scheme. Separately, an analog Rydberg simulator performs phase estimation of ground-state energies and gaps for up to 19 atoms via Loschmidt echoes. Peripheral items cover Krotov control of GHZ-type XXZ states, bosonic Fock-state stabilization, an Fe2+:forsterite qubit and Majorana-based reservoir computing.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
